Z||000002||fierospeeder||05-22-2001||03:25 PM||||i know some atvs and the goldwings have reverse.  <P>I would try looking on ebay for engines.  Unless you want to try in back of a motorcycle magazine for ads dealing with used parts.  motorcycle junkyards are not really popular.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-22-2001||06:27 PM||||Sure they are.  Try <A HREF="http://www.cycletherapy.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cycletherapy.com</A>  for a start.  The only MC engines I know of that have reverse are the Wings (like fierospeeder said).  Only problem with that is that I'm guessing you're looking for a high revving engine.  If so, the 1500 in the Wing isn't what you're looking for.  If you have gobs of extra cash, you might consider the motor in the new Wing (1800cc).  It's a much higher revving motor and still has reverse.  Best of luck finding one used, though as the bike just came out this year.  A new motor will set you back around 7 grand (not counting the tranny and you can't use the 1500 tranny with the 1800 motor).  If you are independantly wealthy, you could always go for the "real" Indy V8 (that'll only set you back about 50 grand USD).<P>MM||||reg||1
